== Walkthrough ==

=== Burning Soul of the Pious ===
In the depths of [[Splitpaw Lair]] (#6 on the map) you can find [[Brother Hayle]], a cleric of [[Rodcet Nife]]. He has been captured by the [[Split Paw Clan]] gnolls, and is a key figure in the [[Zimel's Blades (SoulFire)|quest]] for the Paladin blade [[Soulfire]]. Open his cell door wth the switch on the wall outside.

After you complete the [[Zimel's Blades (SoulFire)|Zimel's Blades]] quest and obtain the [[Soulfire]] you'll have options. If your active loadout has [[Paladin]] and [[Shadowknight]], then you'll receive a message. To proceed with the Torrid Corruptor quest, murder [[Brother Hayle]]. He drops the [[Burning Soul of the Pious]], which contains a message for murderers like you. Right click the Soul in your inventory (you must right-click the soul in order to progress the quest) to receive a message from a greater power:

: As you stare into the fading embers within your palm, you are haunted by the visage of Brother Hayle and your decision to slay him. What temptation drove you to this madness? Within moments, a voice fills your head. "You've done well. This loathsome soul sought to spread their own piety into the minds of gnolls, disgracing the blessing of decay I've bestowed upon them." As the voice speaks, you feel a churn in your stomach as if you are about to be sick. "If you wish to understand your actions, seek out my servant, Lord Grimrot. Bestow upon them my gift through your hands, a dark reaver, and a token of your loyalty, the soul you have claimed. Only though them will you learn the truth."

=== Burning Soul of the Pestilent ===
Make sure you have at least Kindly faction with the [[Bloodsabers]]. [[Guard Shilster's Stout]] is a quick but more expensive method, and the [[Gharin's Note (evil)]] quest is slower but more economical. 

* For [[Guard Shilster's Stout]], give 5 gold per turnin to [[Guard Shilster]] (1380, -2764) in [[Northern Plains of Karana|North Karana]]. It takes about ~3000 gold to max out all of his factions.
* Find the [[a ghoul cavalier|ghoul cavalier]] in the Dead Side area of [[Lower Guk]] and take the [[A Dark Reaver|Dark Reaver]] from it. 

Find [[Lord Grimrot]] (1377, 1172) by the skeletons in [[South Karana]]. There's a living and undead version with the same name. '''The turn-in requires the living version.''' It's rumored to be a 3.2-hour spawn. One of the fastest ways to spawn Lord Grimrot is to make a non-respawning instance during daytime between 6am and 6pm. Use <code><nowiki>/time</nowiki></code> to see the in-game time.

Turn in the clicked version of [[Burning Soul of the Pious]] and [[Dark Reaver]] to the living version of Lord Grimrot.
: Lord Grimrot says, 'You have served me well. You may yet prove useful to my master.'
